> I have two questions.
>  1. Is my decision to choose the var_fixed model over the var_free model sound?

I would say yes.

>  2. Was there some other way I could have fitted the model to overcome

>     the negative variance estimation issue

You could use bounded estimation. Either use the argument bounds =
"pos.var" (forces all variances to be non-negative), or bounds =
"standard" (upper/lower bounds for many parameters).

Yves.

